    // Moonlight Jellies 
    /*
    Did you know out of the thousands of jellyfish species, only about a hundred are strong enough to seriously harm or inflict pain in humans?
    Though, don't get me wrong, if you get stung by ANY jellyfish, you should still see a medical professional--preferably me, but...
    Sorry, I really don't know where I was going with this.

    Out of all my time in the valley, I'm surprised I haven't done more research on the moonlight jellies. 
    Though, I did hear through the grapevine that moonlight jellies in some places are considered an aphrodisiac due to their mystical properties.
    I... Don't think I could ethically recommend trying that at home though.
    
    It really pains me when I hear others spreading that dreaded myth of pee soothing jellyfish stings.
    There's simply far too many species of jellyfish for that to be a reliable treatment. Not to mention how urine is simply just human waste... Such a disgusting myth if I do say so myself.
    In the actual case you get stung, you ought to instead see a doctor for proper first aid. Often picking the visible tentacles will immediately soothe pain. 

    ---

    Did  you know there are certain species of jellyfish that are functionally immortal?
    Really makes you think if we could ever reach that point...
    I mean, wouldn't it be nice? A true eternity spent with those you love...

    ...$l
    Y'know, I have a million facts and interesting stories about these jellyfish just swarming in my mind but...
    Yoba, {{LPetName}}, have I ever told you just how {{LDescript}} you are under the moonlight? 

    I almost wonder what these jellyfish would look like from an aerial point of view...
    Though, probably wouldn't be nearly as lovely as you, {{LPetName}}.
    */
